Shotloop.app bundles two third-party programs, run as separate
processes and under their own licenses:

- Node.js (https://nodejs.org), MIT License and the licenses of its
  dependencies, as listed in its LICENSE file.
- FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), a static build with libx264 by Martin
  Riedl (https://ffmpeg.martin-riedl.de), under the GNU General Public
  License version 3. Its source code is available from
  https://ffmpeg.org/download.html and from the build's page.

The 2D renderer bundles three.js 0.187.0 (https://threejs.org), MIT
License (engine/shotloop/vendor/three-0.187.0/LICENSE), which a 2D
shot's page loads to draw a part in 3D.

The voice-over (voice/) bundles two libraries, loaded into its Node.js
process:

- sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), Apache License 2.0,
  with the ONNX Runtime it ships.
- ONNX Runtime (https://onnxruntime.ai), MIT License.

Its speech models are not part of this distribution: they are downloaded
on first use, each under its own license:

- Kokoro 82M by hexgrad (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M),
  Apache License 2.0, in the int8 packaging of sherpa-onnx with its
  lexicons (English).
- CosyVoice 2 (CosyVoice2-0.5B) by FunAudioLLM
  (https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice), Apache License 2.0
  (Chinese). It runs in its own Python install, also downloaded on first
  use: Python 3.10 and pinned packages (voice/py/requirements.txt, among
  them PyTorch, BSD-3-Clause; Transformers, Apache-2.0; Whisper, MIT),
  set up with uv (MIT or Apache-2.0), Matcha-TTS (MIT) and the text
  normalization rules of WeTextProcessing (Apache-2.0). Its stock voice is
  CosyVoice's own sample recording.
- Supertonic 3 by Supertone (https://huggingface.co/Supertone/supertonic-3),
  OpenRAIL-M License; voice/src/supertonic.mjs adapts its MIT-licensed
  Node.js example (https://github.com/supertone-inc/supertonic).

Third-party material that projects may use is not part of this
distribution: the CC0 asset packs listed in engine/assets/README.md
(Kenney, Poly Haven, Quaternius) are downloaded, not committed, and keep
their own licenses. Music beds are synthesized by engine/shotloop/synth.mjs
and contain no samples.

Map data: engine/shotloop/world-110m.json (the countries the map style
draws) is derived from Natural Earth 1:110m Admin 0 countries
(https://www.naturalearthdata.com), which is in the public domain, as
packaged in world-atlas 2.0.2 by Mike Bostock (https://github.com/topojson/world-atlas),
ISC License.
